------------------------------------------
1- PROJECT MISSIONS
------------------------------------------
    - *Build  a lightweight, completely free tool to help self-learners* or people
who study under the Marugoto method to master Japanese (grammar structures,
verb conjugations, vocabulary, kanji and kana).
    - *Keep the experience free of ads, distractions and paywalls* that oftenly
difficult students' learning process.
    - The project was created as a *review tool*, despite this, we encourage the
explanation inside the lessons to allow low-resources persons (who don't
have access to a japanese academy) to learn using the program.
    - *International and language-friendly*, thanks to the structure, allowing 
everyone to upload the translation to other languages quickly.

------------------------------------------
2- HOW THE PROGRAM WORKS?
------------------------------------------
    - The program uses PyQt5 as its core to display interfaces and JSON files as
    local database (lessons, tests, UI translations, configuration files)
    This allows the program to be completely independant of external servers, 
    offering an offline app for users.
    - The learning module is based on tracking on users' reviewed lessons and SRS 
    (Spaced-Repetition System), paired it with integrated exams, verbs glossary, 
    and integrated vocabulary for lessons.
    - ALL translations can be done by: copying the preferred language json file and
    translating texts, buttons, meanings... etc. The program will check on the language
    in "config.json" and load the selected one. It's important to notice that all
    translations must have support for every text found, or the program may crash
    (notify the user and development team if the program only covers certain parts or lessons)

------------------------------------------
3- CORE PROGRAMMING PRINCIPLES
------------------------------------------
    - *Simplicity Over Cleverness*: Write readable, clear code over complex, 
    over-engineered abstractions.
    - *Zero External Dependencies*: Prefer standard libraries where possible 
    to keep building/compiling trivial.
    - *Performance & Footprint*: Instant boot time and minimal memory usage. Optimization
    is a clue core of the program and the reason why Python was selected.
    - *Integration of comments in code*: Keep in mind there's other programmers working,
    they also need to understand your code to help you optimize, add or substract. Try to
    comment of parts of the code to explain. Silly comments are allowed too! 

------------------------------------------
4- ORGANIZATION AND WORKFLOW
------------------------------------------
In the files of the program you will find the next structure you must mantain
    /data           - Anything related to resources, databases and media (fonts, images...)
    --> /content    - Refers to the lessons (vocabulary, tests...) and verbs glossary
        ----> /lessons  - they're stored as "lesson_n" and so on
    --> /local      - local files that keep the program working (language, fonts...)
        ----> /fonts    - As the name says, you'll store the fonts here in preferable ".ttf"
        ----> /images   - Anything related to icons, character images, etc.
        ----> /languages - Here you find the json files you can use as templates
    /development    - Here you find the TOS, this manifesto file and control/objective list
    credits.txt     - Please, if you're using external media (like icons), add them here!
    main.py         - Here's the base program structure made with PyQt5
    conjugation.py  - A list of conjugation functions, necessary due to japanese
    notifier.py     - It helps with the SRS method, executes once per day



